In article <1993Feb12.102413.14222@leland.Stanford.EDU> trump@leland.Stanford.EDU (Michael Jason Lewis) writes:
>After seeing the earlier post about the Tsurugi and hazily remembering a post
>a while back about the Mitre of Holiness, I have a question:
>
>Is it possible to wish for these things?

Yes, and since this info is pretty safe from abuse, it is very bad to wish
for any item that is not for your class, since it will shock the bejeezus
out of you, and you will be forced to drop it.  So, unless you like an
uncarryable, deadly-to-the-touch item, forget wishing for another class's
artifact...

>
>Also...Vorpal Blade is sentient, or at least it shocks you if you're not co-
>aligned.  Found one in a shop, and I picked it up to kill the shopkeeper, and
>it nailed me.  I was hurting, so I have no idea how much damage it did...but it
>was enough.

I think it's alignment.  When you're very aligned with any alignment and
attempt to wield powerful weapons of different alignments, you will be
shocked.  I believe that Stormy, Mjolly, Vorpy, and Excalibur all do this,
but I shall check further on this.
